// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/t27os/queen_board.t27 -- the live board of the Q page: see the Queen work and improve the system in GOD MODE
; Owner, 2026-10-20: in GOD MODE we must SEE her working and improving the system live. Data model only (pure,
; tested); the window draws it later. Everything on the page is a widget (nested rects, see LAYOUT). Closes #11275.
; ASCII only (L3), English only (LANG-EN).
; --
; DRY: nothing is copied. Gaps, priority, why-not and the caps come from evolve.t27 (used); the ring and its
; controls from queen.t27 (used); the lamp aggregates from domain_pulse.t27 (used); the counters of the meter from
; agent_parts.t27 (used); the packer from dash.t27 (used, read only). Only genuinely new data lives here: the feed
; kinds, the board rows, the meter's provenance and the page layout.
; --
; WHAT THE HOST MUST FEED (this file runs no command), and when:
;   RING      the queen.t27 ring (8 u64 events), read from memory each frame; no command.
;   LANE LOG  lines "sec QB_TAB kind QB_TAB letter QB_TAB text LF", kind = FK_* below (task opened, lane started, test
;             verdict, landed); written by the host when a lane changes state; text is a profile name or a short
;             sentence, NEVER a key (profile_ok refuses a key-looking text). Newest line last in the file.
;   PANEL     the evolve.t27 Panel (masks), the in-flight mask, running, started_hour, risk mask+class: each time
;             the panel refreshes (same cadence as the lamps).
;   LAMPS     `git log --since=7.days --name-only --format=%x1e%H%x1f%ct%x1f%s` plus the red-path list, ONCE A
;             MINUTE, only while the window is open (lamp_refresh_due). domain_pulse.t27 is used directly.
;   METER     six counters at each refresh, commands in meter_cmd; the first refresh after LOCAL midnight is the
;             "start of day" snapshot (snapshot_due).
;   SAFETY    tasks this hour, agents running, god flag, and the key tier name as a TEXT ENUM from the keys lane
;             (never a key, never a prefix of a key).

